Apple today announced an upcoming product launch that will take place on Tuesday, October 13. We are expecting Apple's announcement to focus on new smart home products, including the long-rumored smart home hub, a new <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/apple-tv/">Apple TV</a> 4K, and a refreshed <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/homepod-mini/">HomePod mini</a>.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/apple-welcome-home-event.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="900" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1069479" /><br/>
The home hub is an all-new device that's like a cross between an <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ipad/">iPad</a> and a <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/homepod/">HomePod</a>. It's rumored to have a 6-inch square display, and it's designed as a multi-person device to control smart home products, place <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/facetime/">FaceTime</a> calls, watch videos, get news and weather information, stay up to date on calendar events, and more. It will integrate with <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/siri/">Siri</a> AI, and voice will be the main method of interaction.<br/>
<br/>
Apple envisions people installing a hub in multiple rooms in the house. There will be a version meant to be mounted on the wall and a version with a half-dome speaker base, similar in design to the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/imac/">iMac</a> G4. A camera and a presence sensor will detect when a person is in the room, and the device will be able to tell who it is to show a customized interface with widgets and apps. Pricing could be around &#36;350.<br/>
