The &zwnj;HomePod mini&zwnj; is going to get new colors, an N1 networking chip for improved Wi-Fi and Bluetooth, and a faster S-series processor that will support &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; AI. The &zwnj;Apple TV&zwnj; 4K is going to get an A19 or A19 Pro chip, a RAM upgrade, the same N1 chip as the &zwnj;HomePod mini&zwnj;, and an upgraded &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; Remote.<br/>
<br/>
There is an <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/macbook-ultra/">OLED</a> <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ipad-mini/">iPad mini</a> in development, and it could come during the home event. The &zwnj;iPad mini&zwnj; is expected to be more water-resistant with a faster chip and the first &zwnj;OLED&zwnj; display in a smaller tablet size.<br/>
<br/>
Timing on the October 13 product launch is unknown, and it is also unclear if there will be an event component or if the devices will debut via press release. Some members of the media have been invited to an "Apple Experience" set to take place in Tribeca, New York on October 13 at 9:00 a.m. Attendees will likely get hands-on time with the new products Apple introduces. <br/>
<br/>
Rumors suggest Apple has several Macs coming before the end of the year, but those could be introduced at later in the year instead of during the home product launch.<br/>
